From 464c44cc8974c2b868938f6266cfb5e3c1c587ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 10:39:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] NVIDIA: SAUCE: PCI: harden MediaTek Power Wrap system
 sleep

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167887

MediaTek Power Wrap removes configuration and MMIO access for a complete
PCI host segment. Restrict that coordination to system sleep, where PCI
devices and native port services can be quiesced as a unit. Runtime host
gating cannot safely contain a failed D0 restore while drivers, BAR users,
hotplug, and configuration-space interfaces remain active.

Track all Root Ports belonging to a host and issue the D3 request only
after every direct root-bus function is a managed Root Port in D3cold. Veto
host gating for wake paths, unsafe hotplug configurations, or any untracked
function. Serialize final-port aggregation across hosts and revalidate the
complete hierarchy while holding the PCI topology locks.

Run PCIe port-service suspend callbacks for managed ports. Quiesce pending
PME work and prevent the shared PME IRQ from touching configuration space
after its no-IRQ state is set. Restore the host to D0 before the first PCI
resume access. If a D3 timeout leaves host state ambiguous, or D0 cannot be
confirmed, stop execution instead of returning to PCI with potentially
inaccessible configuration space and BARs.

This folds the PCI fixes identified during NV-Kernels review.

